%!PS
% Test content for poem.ps: the shortest poem it takes (two lines), dark theme.
% Ezra Pound, "In a Station of the Metro" (1913), in the public domain.
% `psanim check poem-pound.ps` runs poem.ps with this content.
/tpl (poem.ps) component
/film /tpl << /Params <<
  /look /midnight
  /heading (In a Station of the Metro)
  /poet (Ezra Pound, 1913)
  /poem [ (The apparition of these faces in the crowd;)
          (Petals on a wet, black bough.) ]
  /notes [
    [ 0 (apparition) (image)
      (A ghostly word for ordinary travellers: faces seen for an instant in a dark station.) ]
    [ 1 (Petals on a wet, black bough) (turn)
      (No verb joins the two lines. The second sits beside the first, and the eye makes the comparison.) ]
  ]
  /reading (One image laid over another: a crowd becomes a branch after rain, and a moment underground becomes something seen in nature.)
>> >> instance
<< /Size [1280 720] /Duration /film componentduration /FPS 30 >> animation
/scene { /film << /After /hold >> place } def
